  "notes": "A compound verb meaning to cut something into portions and distribute or separate them. Most commonly used for food but also applies figuratively to breaking down problems or topics.\n\nFORMS:\n{切|き}る (to cut) + {分|わ}ける (to divide/separate).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Takes を for the thing being cut and divided\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{切|き}り{分|わ}けている describes the ongoing action of cutting and dividing.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ケーキを{切|き}り{分|わ}ける: cut a cake into slices\n- {肉|にく}を{切|き}り{分|わ}ける: carve meat into portions\n- {均等|きんとう}に{切|き}り{分|わ}ける: cut into equal portions\n- {問題|もんだい}を{切|き}り{分|わ}ける: break a problem into parts (figurative)",
